      "claim": "A panel of trained non-experts following an explicit checklist will not reliably outperform a single domain expert, because the checklist acts as an information bottleneck. Genuine reliability gain can be isolated within a single evaluation by introducing adversarial perturbations (rephrased inputs, edge-cases): genuine gain degrades gracefully under perturbation while checklist-compliance tracks the right answer only under input invariance and collapses under distributional shift.",
